# {{lb|en|US}} A [[concession]] made by a [[labor]] [[union]] in the course of [[negotiation]]s.
# {{lb|en|frequently|in the plural}} An [[idea]] from a [[talk]], [[presentation]], etc., that the [[listener]] or [[reader]] should [[remember]] and [[consider]].<ref>{{cite-web |author=Joe Miller| title=Davos jargon: A crime against the English language?| url=http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/business-42791874| work=BBC News| publisher=BBC| date=24 January 2018}}</ref>
#* '''2008''', Carol A. E. Bentley, ''Beat The Recession: Proven Marketing Tactics'', Volume 1, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=SahF7RdpWzkC&pg=PA363&lpg=PA363&dq=%22takeaway%22|%22takeaways%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&source=bl&ots=Y0AaQEXPEZ&sig=YI7EKKMnE7Ogr-I3Haza0tI3NfQ&hl=en&sa=X&ei=7yV4UPqvBsmsiAexoIGgDg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22takeaway%22|%22takeaways%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 363],
